@startuml
title How the DEFENSE checkbox reaches every layer
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #1F4E79
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F2F6FA
  BorderColor #1F4E79
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  DiamondBorderColor #1F4E79
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #9E9D24
}
start
:Presenter ticks **DEFENSE**
(presenter.py: gr.Checkbox);
:run_btn.click(do_run, [request, level, defense])
-> do_run(req, lvl, dfn);
:ctx.agent(int(lvl), bool(dfn))
(common.py AppContext.agent);
:Defense(enabled=True, allowlist, store)
handed to ShopDeskAgent(defense=...);
fork
  :**1 Flag**
  agent.run -> defense.flags_for(ticket)
  -> detect_instructions(message);
fork again
  :**2 Fence**
  agent.run -> defense.render_ticket(ticket)
  -> fence() with random boundary;
fork again
  :**3 Prompt**
  system_prompt(defense=True)
  -> strict base + DEFENDED rules,
  no NAIVE_TOOLS / REALISTIC_INTAKE;
fork again
  :**4 Policy limits**
  agent.run -> set_scope(tickets, request)
  _process_calls -> check_tool_call
  -> _policy(name, inputs);
fork again
  :**5 Approval gate**
  check_tool_call -> "approve"
  for irreversible tools;
end fork
:Every layer writes a trace line
(defense / block / approval);
stop
note right
  Unticked: Defense(enabled=False).
  flags_for returns [], render_ticket returns plain text,
  check_tool_call returns allow for everything,
  and the prompt is the realistic (or strict) naive one.
  Resume after an approval uses run.defense,
  not the current checkbox (presenter.py do_resume).
end note
@enduml
